[
  {
    "filename": "jiaocaineedrop_eng-45646.pdf_30.pdf",
    "page_index": 30,
    "core_content": {
      "parsing_res_list": [
        {
          "block_label": "header",
          "block_content": "LibreTexts\"",
          "block_bbox": [
            242,
            111,
            524,
            161
          ],
          "block_id": 0,
          "block_order": null
        },
        {
          "block_label": "chart",
          "block_content": "Risk \nLikelihood Impact \nVulnerability Threat \nCapability Opportunity Intent \n",
          "block_bbox": [
            531,
            278,
            2017,
            1316
          ],
          "block_id": 1,
          "block_order": null
        },
        {
          "block_label": "figure_title",
          "block_content": "Figure1.4.1.1:DoDRiskModel.(\"DoDRiskModelbyUnknown,U.S.NavalAcademy-CyberScience Deptis inthePublic Domain,CCo)\n",
          "block_bbox": [
            310,
            1405,
            2224,
            1483
          ],
          "block_id": 2,
          "block_order": null
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "In thecyberdomain,justas inalldomains,thereare variousfactors thatgo intoassessingrisk.RiskAssessmentcan be viewed as a function with inputs,a process,and outputs. In generalrisk is viewed as afunction oflikelihood ofoccurrenceofan event and impact of an event, risk( likelihood, impact ).\n",
          "block_bbox": [
            205,
            1510,
            2327,
            1658
          ],
          "block_id": 3,
          "block_order": 1
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Intuitively,ifweincreasethelikelihoodofa negativeeventoccurring,theriskseverityincreases,andvice versa.This is alsothe case with impact,if the impact of a negative event occurring increases,the risk severity increases.",
          "block_bbox": [
            205,
            1690,
            2324,
            1787
          ],
          "block_id": 4,
          "block_order": 2
        },
        {
          "block_label": "paragraph_title",
          "block_content": "Likelihood ofOccurrence ",
          "block_bbox": [
            208,
            1828,
            669,
            1864
          ],
          "block_id": 5,
          "block_order": 3
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Likelihoodofoccurrencecan be decomposed into twomain components:threatandvulnerability. Threatisanycircumstanceor eventthathasthepotentialtoadversely impactour system. Threatcanbeadversarial(purposely causedby a person)ornonadversarial(causedbyanaccidentor naturaleventsuchasahurricane).Vulnerabilityrepresentsa weaknessinaninformation system that can be exploited,often by an adversarial threat actor.\n",
          "block_bbox": [
            205,
            1899,
            2325,
            2099
          ],
          "block_id": 6,
          "block_order": 4
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Notallvulnerabilitiesareequal,therearefactorsthat wecanassess avulnerability with.Theriskassessmentteamwillaskand answer questions such as (OWASP):",
          "block_bbox": [
            206,
            2129,
            2324,
            2221
          ],
          "block_id": 7,
          "block_order": 5
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Discoverable)Howeasy is itforanadversary to discover thevulnerability?",
          "block_bbox": [
            216,
            2254,
            1502,
            2293
          ],
          "block_id": 8,
          "block_order": 6
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Exploitable) How easy is it for anadversary to exploit the vulnerability?",
          "block_bbox": [
            218,
            2309,
            1452,
            2348
          ],
          "block_id": 9,
          "block_order": 7
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Awareness) Howwellknown is thevulnerability?",
          "block_bbox": [
            220,
            2361,
            1094,
            2400
          ],
          "block_id": 10,
          "block_order": 8
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Detectable) How likely is anexploitto bedetected?",
          "block_bbox": [
            218,
            2413,
            1120,
            2453
          ],
          "block_id": 11,
          "block_order": 9
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Just as vulnerabilities,threats arealso assessedusing various factors. Theriskassessment team willaskandanswerquestions such as(OWASP):",
          "block_bbox": [
            205,
            2488,
            2327,
            2581
          ],
          "block_id": 12,
          "block_order": 10
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Capability) Howtechnicallyskilled isanadversary?",
          "block_bbox": [
            216,
            2614,
            1130,
            2653
          ],
          "block_id": 13,
          "block_order": 11
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Capability) How much does theadversary know about the target system?",
          "block_bbox": [
            218,
            2667,
            1465,
            2706
          ],
          "block_id": 14,
          "block_order": 12
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Opportunity) Does theadversary have the resources (technology)to exploit a vulnerability?",
          "block_bbox": [
            218,
            2721,
            1758,
            2762
          ],
          "block_id": 15,
          "block_order": 13
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Opportunity) Is theadversary in a position to exploit a vulnerability?",
          "block_bbox": [
            219,
            2774,
            1397,
            2814
          ],
          "block_id": 16,
          "block_order": 14
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Intent) Howmotivated is anadversary tofindand exploita vulnerability?",
          "block_bbox": [
            221,
            2826,
            1470,
            2866
          ],
          "block_id": 17,
          "block_order": 15
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "(Intent) Does the actor performing the exploit intend harm?",
          "block_bbox": [
            220,
            2880,
            1229,
            2920
          ],
          "block_id": 18,
          "block_order": 16
        },
        {
